rows.masked_reference_solution:
When using the distributive property, we add the product of $M$ and $2x$ to the product of $M$ and $N$:
\begin{align*}
M(2x+N) &= M\cdot 2x+M\cdot N\\
&= \boxed{Ox+P}
\end{align*}

rows.reference_solution:
When using the distributive property, we add the product of 16 and $2x$ to the product of 16 and 5:
\begin{align*}
16(2x+5) &= 16\cdot 2x+16\cdot 5\\
&= \boxed{32x+80}
\end{align*}

